# Within checks/, only the parts later weeks actually depend on are tracked
# (the phantom test suite + the vendored official scorer). validate.py and
# its run outputs are Week-1-specific verification, not needed by git.
checks/validate.py
checks/outputs/

# Per-run logs. Written fresh on every execution and named by date, so they
# accumulate one file per script per day — exactly the pattern CLAUDE.md
# Section 5.4 rules out. They stay on disk as the debugging record for the
# current run (Section 5.6 still requires them), they just aren't history:
# every number they contain is already in the QC CSVs and the subject index,
# which ARE tracked and carry provenance sidecars.
#
# Applied uniformly, including the two Week 1 logs under metadata/outputs/ that
# predate this rule — those were untracked with `git rm --cached` in the same
# commit that added this line, and remain on disk.
*.log
